<article class="env-example" id="09BJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09BJ">Example <span data-tag="09BJ">61.6.3</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $T$ be a profinite topological space. There exists an ind-Zariski ring map $k \to A$ such that $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is homeomorphic to $T$. Namely, just apply Lemma <a href="/tag/097D" data-tag="097D">61.6.2</a> to $T \to \pi _0(\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)) = \{ *\} $. In fact, in this case we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \text{Map}(T_ i, k)  \]
</div>
  <p> whenever we write $T = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits T_ i$ as a filtered limit with each $T_ i$ finite. </p>
</article>